index 82a9c1d..882674b 100644
--- a/docs/API.md
+++ b/docs/API.md
@@ -210,16 +210,43 @@ Changes are announced to the channel's members as `MODE` lines from the server a
 This endpoint joins every connected client of an account to channels, with the same semantics as `SAJOIN` (channel modes and bans don't apply; a channel that doesn't exist is created). An always-on client with no attached session is not joined. The request is a JSON object with fields:
 
 * `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `nick`: string, optional, instead of `accountName`: join only the client with this nick (logged in or not)
 * `channels`: list of strings, the channels to join
 
 The response is a JSON object with fields:
 
-* `success`: boolean, whether the request succeeded (`true` with `clients` 0 if nobody is logged into the account)
+* `success`: boolean, whether the request succeeded (`true` with `clients` 0 if nobody is logged into the account, or no client has the nick)
 * `clients`: number, how many connected clients of the account were joined
 * `joined`: list of strings, the channels every client is now in
 * `failed`: object, maps each channel that couldn't be joined to the reason
 * `errorCode`: string, optional: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST` for an invalid account name
 
+`/v1/channel_ensure`
+--------------------
+
+This endpoint makes sure a channel exists and is registered, for channels an external system keeps for the whole network. A channel that doesn't exist is created with no members (it stays, being registered); a channel that isn't registered is registered to `founder`; a channel registered to someone else is left alone. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `channel`: string, the channel
+* `founder`: string, the account to register it to (it need not exist yet)
+* `setTopic`: boolean, optional: also set the topic to `topic`
+* `topic`: string, optional, the topic (empty clears it)
+* `topicSetBy`: string, optional, shown as the topic's setter (default `API`)
+* `noExpire`: boolean, optional: exempt the channel from `channels.registration.expire-after` (like `CS SET #channel EXPIRY OFF`)
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: boolean
+* `created`: boolean, whether the channel was created
+* `registered`: boolean, whether the channel was registered to `founder` by this call
+* `founder`: string, the channel's founder now
+* `topicChanged`: boolean, whether the topic was changed
+* `errorCode`: string, optional: `INVALID_FOUNDER`, `INVALID_CHANNEL`, `CHANNEL_PURGED`, `CONFUSABLE_NAME` or `DEFCON`
+
+`/v1/channel_drop`
+------------------
+
+This endpoint unregisters a channel if it is registered to `founder` (nobody is kicked; the channel goes away when it empties). The request is a JSON object with fields `channel` and `founder`. The response has `success`, `dropped` (boolean) and `founder` (the founder now, when it wasn't dropped).
+
 `/v1/ns/saregister`
 -------------------
 
